      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buckskin_Joe"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1958, Buckskin Joe owners opened the park to tourists, turning the set into a living western attraction.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buckskin_Joe"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The park’s general store, the only original Buckskin Joe building, was owned by Colorado pioneer Horace Tabor.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buckskin_Joe"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Every October, Buckskin Joe staff converted the town into a haunted attraction, capitalizing on its real haunted history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
